WEBVTT

3.1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.325
Let's answer one. Open the Barton Hills request.

3.2
00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:10.042
At the top you'll see the job, delivery or pickup, and the date.

3.3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:17.525
Below that, each line is a plant we need: the quantity, the size and the name. Our notes sit under the plant.

3.4
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:23.117
Prices we already have on file are filled in. Just correct any that have changed.

3.5
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.025
Now set a status for each line.

3.6
00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:31.142
If you have them all, choose Available. That's it, it saves straight away.

3.7
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.225
Only have some? Choose Partial Quantity, type how many you can supply, and add a note if it helps.

3.8
00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:45.867
Can you get them in? Choose Can Order or Arriving Soon, and tell us when.

3.9
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.650
A line with a purple box still needs a price. Click it and type your unit price.

3.10
00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:02.467
Everything saves as you go, so you can stop and come back any time.

3.11
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:08.483
The coloured counts at the top add up your answers, and you can click one to filter the lines.
